 like you  really like real estate if you own two  houses and on a plot of land that you  want to build on so I would just make  sure before you know cleaning too that  you're you're really excited but real  estate you think you can do you know  invest a lot of time and energy into  that and that's following your heart  the last bit of advice is if you're  gonna have a job as for all  entrepreneurs if you're you know  thinking of starting a new business if  you're if you're going to take a job try  to take a job that gives you more than  money try to take a job where you can  learn something from it  so look at the job here and now you know  if you're going to have a job  try to use something from that job that  you can later implement it to put into  your own business so is there something  from the job you're you're in now that  will help you learn for when you run in  your own business maybe there's extra  roles or responsibilities you can take  on to give you that knowledge and to  give you the training without you know  wasting your own money on it that can  then help you later build your business  so a quick example of this I have a  really kind of jobs but when I was in  university I was already running my own  business and I used my courses to help  me build my business so I created my own  course in you know small business and  all my marketing assignments all related  around my business that I was currently  running so I was able to use the  resources of my university to help me  plan and grow my business so it's a  great way to be able to leverage stuff  that you're already doing to help you  you know develop your skills and later  be able to run your business more  effectively so I hope that helps if you  guys liked the video please give it a  thumbs up I'd also love to hear feedback  if you want to leave a comment below the  video and stay tuned for the next  episode  you
 

